# What does not belong on the public site.
#
# Found by fetching it: https://pre-call-swart.vercel.app/assets/model.test.js
# answered 200. Every test file in this repository has been served in
# production since the first deploy — around 200KB nobody loads, plus the
# fixtures and the reasoning inside them, on a product that is sold.
#
# weight.test.js said in prose that test files "are not shipped and are not
# counted". The second half was true. The first half was not, and nothing
# checked it, because a file being deployed and a file being loaded are
# different things and only the second one was ever measured.
#
# There is no build step here, so this list is the only thing separating
# what is written from what is served. markup.test.js asserts it stays
# complete — and it now asserts the whole rule rather than half of it: every
# file in the repository is either matched here or matched by an allowlist of
# what the product actually is. The earlier version only checked test files,
# and a docs/ directory added later was about to be published with every
# check green.

# tests — every suite, wherever it lives
*.test.js

# The key minter, and operator tooling generally. It holds no secret — the
# checksum it uses ships in assets/pc-gate.js on every page load — but a page
# that mints licence-shaped keys has no reason to be reachable from the
# internet, and with no build step it would sit at a public URL.
tools/

# Research method, not product. The protocol for the first ten participants is
# written to be run by the operator, and a page describing how the product will
# be tested has no reason to answer 200 to the people being tested.
docs/

# The target contract, not the shipped page. landing/post-call.html states what
# POST-CALL is supposed to be able to do, and landing.test.js holds every one of
# those claims against a product test. Until they all pass, the page describes a
# product that does not exist yet — and a page like that answering 200 is the
# exact failure the contract was written to prevent. The page carries
# noindex,nofollow as well, but that only stops indexing: the URL would still
# answer, and a link pasted into WhatsApp does not care about robots meta.
# Serving it is one line — move it to SERVED in markup.test.js — and that line
# is the release decision.
landing/

# repository furniture
.github/
LICENSE
README.md

# Nothing leaves this behind for us either. assets/weight.test.js fails the run
# if it appears in the repo root, because it would deploy exactly as it sits.
node_modules/
